extraction_notes: "WB9 South America 2 printed 135-137 (cache p135-p137, page_offset 0). The introduction starts on printed 135; abilities, skills, equipment, money and cybernetics are printed 136; the Blood Lizard R.C.C. begins at the top of printed 137, so the class block ends on 136. Printed 136 checked against a 150 dpi render; OCR and render agree. No master-blood-rider class was in production on 2026-09-25. || CATEGORY: occ. The heading on printed 135 reads Master Blood Rider R.C.C., and the Blood Rider''s ability 2 on printed 134 also calls it an R.C.C., but the block itself is headed O.C.C. Abilities and Bonuses and O.C.C. Skills, prints O.C.C. Related Skills and Attribute Requirements (an O.C.C.''s minimums, not rolled attributes), and describes a trained human psychic of the Blood Rider clans rather than a race. The R.C.C. in the heading is read as a slip. || XP: the Master Blood Rider ladder on printed 192, read off a render, as briefed; stored as given. || GROUP: psychic, as the Blood Rider. No sdc_base or mdc_base is printed (+4D6 S.D.C. is a pool bonus), so men_of_arms: true - a cavalry warrior with harsher physical training than the ordinary rider (the Psi-Slinger/Psi-Stalker precedent). || RACE: human, as the Blood Rider; race_restrictions only none. || PSIONICS: master. Granted at first level: Mind Block, Telepathy, Levitation, Telekinesis and Telekinesis (Super) by catalog name; Telekinetic Levitation (Special) and Personal Telekinetic Force Field (Special) are this class''s own powers, not catalog rows, so they are special_abilities with their I.S.P. costs (the survey''s decision for this book). Plus two powers from each of Healing, Physical and Sensitive (three starting groups, 6 picks). Two more from any category including Super at every new level (schedule 2-15); Psi-Sword cannot be taken until third level, expressed as a Super except on the level-2 entry. I.S.P. 3D4x10 + M.E., +2D6 per level. || BONUSES: +2 P.S., +2 P.E., +4D6 S.D.C., +2 pull punch, +2 roll with impact, +4 save vs horror factor stored unconditionally. The lizard-back +2 initiative and +1 strike and parry, and the +4 saves while within 100 feet of the mount, are conditional and are special_abilities prose. || SKILLS: Language: Spanish 98; Literacy: Spanish (+20%) as Literacy: Native Language 40+20; Radio: Basic 45+10; Horsemanship (+10%) as Horsemanship: General 40+10 - this class prints no Horsemanship: Exotic Animals line, unlike the Blood Rider, and none is added; Wilderness Survival 30+20; Tracking: Animals as Track & Trap Animals 20+15; Tracking: Humans as Tracking (people) 25+20; Land Navigation 36+10; W.P. Energy Rifle, one archaic W.P. (choice among the ancient W.P.s), one W.P. of choice; Hand to Hand: Expert, to Martial Arts or Assassin (evil) for one other skill each. || RELATED: 6, plus two at level 3 and one at 6, 8, 11 and 14. As the Blood Rider''s list, but Espionage is +10%, and it prints Physical +5% (if applicable), Pilot +5% and Pilot Related +5%, which the Blood Rider''s omits. Military none. Secondary: two at each of levels one, three, six and nine (count 2, schedule 3, 6, 9), same limits without the bonuses. || EQUIPMENT: as the Blood Rider - Claw Armor, one energy weapon and four E-clips, vibro-blade, three archaic or non-energy weapons, riding cloak (hooded-cloak), two traveling-clothes, dress-clothing. Saddle, camping kit and the Blood Lizard mount have no catalog row and are not stubbed. The 30% chance of a techno-wizard weapon and the 30% chance of an additional energy weapon (roll for each) are random and not stored. || MONEY: 1D6x1000 credits; the class is never paired (race_restrictions only none), so class-check''s racial-discard warning does not bite. Not supersedes_race."
---

## Lore

Roughly one Blood Rider in a hundred is born a master psychic. Beyond the bond
with a mount, these riders wield formidable telekinetic power: they can lift
their lizards into impossible leaps, send them running across the empty air,
and wrap themselves in an invisible shield.

The clans keep these masters secret, fearing that already-suspicious outsiders
would turn on them, and train them harder than any other rider while teaching
loyalty to clan, to all Blood Riders and to humanity, in that order. The
pressure breaks some; others come to despise their clans or everyone without
their gifts. Most survive it and give their lives to a single great cause,
whether defending their people, uniting the clans, or something far larger.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'master-blood-rider');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'master-blood-rider';

